{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_66284b0e00cf7a14dc108b705afe5bfa034da2fc06d02a71a59b519c0a7dd31b", "title": "Mount Moriah Cemetery (Fairview, New Jersey)", "text": "Mount Moriah Cemetery is a burial ground in Fairview, Bergen County, New Jersey in the United States, located on the western slopes of the Hudson Palisades, nearby the Fairview Cemetery.", "score": 31.0593}, {"id": "hp_doc_6bbe7f9aca9cea427f67764c74603fe2baba3efc506cdb20ecf4d08530e101b2", "title": "Mount Moriah Cemetery (South Dakota)", "text": "Mount Moriah Cemetery on Mount Moriah in Deadwood, Lawrence County, South Dakota is the burial place of Wild Bill Hickok, Calamity Jane, Sol Star, Seth Bullock and other notable figures of the Wild West. By tradition, the American flag flies over the cemetery 24 hours a day, rather than merely from sunrise to sunset.", "score": 30.8671}, {"id": "hp_doc_a0cb79b4530216eff2c8aa7559fbade142ae46081b7726e41c144c693c9ae1b6", "title": "Mount Moriah Cemetery (Philadelphia)", "text": "Mount Moriah Cemetery is a historic cemetery in southwest Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, along Cobbs Creek. It was incorporated on March 27, 1855 and established by an act of the Pennsylvania Legislature. The cemetery, which originally occupied 54 acre , was among a number of cemeteries established along the \"rural ideal\" popular at that time. An ornate Romanesque entrance and gatehouse were built of brownstone on Islington Lane, today known as Kingsessing Avenue.", "score": 27.9532}], "remaining_searches": 2}
